              "date": "2023-08-23T09:50",
              "author": "PCP",
              "body": "NEW PATIENT - PREVENTIVE\n\nPaige is 22, starting the second year of a master's program here, and wanted a doctor in the area rather than driving back to Vermont. No concerns today. Feels well, sleeping fine, runs and swims.\n\nPMH: none. No hospitalizations.\nPSH: none.\nMeds: none. No supplements.\nAllergies: no known drug allergies.\nFH: mother - hypothyroidism. Father - high blood pressure. No melanoma or autoimmune skin disease in the family that she knows of.\nSH: grad student; lifeguards at a lake beach in the summers. Never smoked, no vaping. Alcohol a drink or two a month. No drugs. Single.\nGyn: regular cycles. Last Pap 6/2022 normal per outside records.\nImms: childhood series, Tdap 2012, HPV series done per old records.\n\nROS: negative in full except as above.\n\nExam: vitals as charted, BMI normal. Well appearing, pleasant. HEENT clear, TMs normal. Neck supple, no thyroid enlargement or nodules. Heart RRR without murmur. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, nontender. Skin without rashes or concerning lesions. No edema. Neuro grossly normal. Mood bright, PHQ-2 0.\n\nA/P: healthy young adult, establishing care.\n- Screening labs: CBC, CMP, lipids, TSH given mom's thyroid history, one-time HIV and hep C, urine GC/CT.\n- Pap due 2025.\n- Flu and COVID in the fall; she'll come in for a nurse visit.\n- Sunscreen talk, she knows the drill from lifeguarding.\nAnnual physical next summer."
            }
