              "body": "Annual. 25 now, finishing her degree this year. Lifeguarding again this summer.\n\nInterval: the back rash came back. She says it showed up last summer too, mid-season, and faded on its own by fall so she never called. This summer it came back over more of her back and shoulders, so she went back to dermatology on 7/29. Scraping positive again per her. Using ketoconazole shampoo daily, about done with the 2 weeks, then they want her to use it monthly through the warm months. We don't have their note - requested today.\n\nNo other concerns. No meds besides the shampoo. NKDA. FH: mom hypothyroid, dad HTN. Never smoker, rare alcohol.\n\nExam: vitals reviewed. Well. Neck, thyroid normal. Heart RRR, no murmur. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, nontender. Skin: upper back and shoulders with faint lighter and darker patches, minimal scale, improving per her. No other rashes. PHQ-2 0.\n\nA/P:\n1. Tinea versicolor, recurrent - on derm's plan, nothing to add. Reasonable to keep the monthly shampoo going in summer.\n2. Preventive - CBC, CMP, lipids, TSH today. Pap up to date (2025). Flu shot in October - nurse visit booked.\nRTC 1 year."
