              "title": "Dermatology Follow-up (date of service 07/29/2026)",
              "date": "2026-08-25T11:20",
              "author": "dermatology",
              "body": "OUTPATIENT DERMATOLOGY - RETURN VISIT\nDate of service: 07/29/2026\n\nHPI: 25-year-old seen here in March 2025 for tinea versicolor of the trunk, treated with ketoconazole shampoo. She reports the eruption came back during summer 2025 and cleared without treatment by autumn. Since early this summer it has returned on the back and shoulders and covers a larger area than before. She calls the spots \"oddly colored.\" No itching or pain.\n\nMedications: none. Allergies: NKDA.\nFamily history: mother hypothyroidism, father hypertension; no melanoma or autoimmune skin disease.\nSocial: graduate student, summer lifeguard. Never smoker, occasional alcohol (1-2 drinks monthly).\n\nExam: numerous hyper- and hypopigmented macules with fine overlying scale across the upper trunk and both shoulders.\n\nKOH (one lesion): short hyphae and spores seen.\n\nImpression: Recurrent tinea versicolor.\n\nPlan:\n1. Ketoconazole 2% shampoo to affected areas, 5-minute contact, daily x 2 weeks.\n2. Then once monthly, May through September, to reduce recurrences.\n3. Pigment may take months to normalize after treatment; this does not mean treatment failure.\n4. Follow up as needed.\n\ncc: primary care\nDermatology"
